<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  TEST APK ONLY. This file lives in `src/androidTest/res`, so it is merged into
  the instrumentation APK and never into the app the user installs. The shipped
  app declares no network security config at all and therefore keeps the
  platform default, which since API 28 is "no cleartext, anywhere".

  WHY IT IS NEEDED

  ThirdPartyIsolationTest and CrossOriginIframeIsolationTest are the evidence for
  BIT-33 §Acceptance 3 and 4. Both work by standing up a real HTTP server on
  loopback (LocalTestServer binds 127.0.0.1:0) and pointing a real HardenedWebView
  at it, because the thing under test is a genuine third-party *origin* — and an
  origin is a scheme, host and port, which `loadData` does not give you and which
  a second port on 127.0.0.1 does.

  targetSdk is 36, so without this the WebView refuses the fixture with
  ERR_CLEARTEXT_NOT_PERMITTED and the page never loads. That failure mode is worse
  than it sounds: a page that never loaded also never finds a bridge, so a probe
  test can go green having exercised nothing. The load assertions in both tests
  are written to catch that (see `assertFixtureRan`), and this config is what stops
  it happening in the first place.

  WHY IT IS SCOPED TO 127.0.0.1

  `cleartextTrafficPermitted="true"` on a bare `base-config` would let the test APK
  talk http to anything, which is a strictly larger hole than the one being opened
  and would also mask a genuine regression — an https-only assertion in a future
  test would stop failing. The permission is therefore attached to the single
  domain the test servers bind to, with `includeSubdomains` off because an IP
  literal has no subdomains.

  `localhost` is listed alongside it because the two are not interchangeable to
  the platform: the config matches on the host string as written in the URL, and
  a future fixture that spells its origin `http://localhost:PORT` would otherwise
  be refused for reasons no one would enjoy tracking down.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <domain-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true">
        <domain includeSubdomains="false">127.0.0.1</domain>
        <domain includeSubdomains="false">localhost</domain>
    </domain-config>
</network-security-config>
